Verse 1:
[Ab]It came upon the midnight clear,
[Db]That glorious [Bb7]song of [Eb/Bb]old,
[Ab]From angels [Db/Ab]bending [Ab]near the earth
[Bbm]To touch their [Eb7]harps of [Ab]gold:
[Ab]“Peace [Cm]on the earth, [Fm/Ab]goodwill to [Ab]men,
[Bbm]From heaven’s [Eb/Bb]all [Ab]gracious [Db/Ab]King;”
[Ab]The world in solemn [Bbm]stillness [Eb7]lay,
[Ab]To hear the angels sing.

Verse 2:
[Ab]Still through the [Db/Ab]cloven [Ab]skies they come,
[Db]With peaceful [Bb7]wings unfurled;
[Ab]And still their heavenly music floats
[Bbm]O'er all the [Eb7]weary [Ab]world:
[Ab]Above [Cm]its sad [Fm/Ab]and lowly [Ab]plains
[Bbm]They bend on [Eb/Bb]hovering [Db/Ab]wing,
[Ab]And ever o'er [Bbm]its Babel [Eb7]sounds
[Ab]The blessed angels sing.

Verse 3:
[Ab]O ye beneath [Db/Ab]life's [Ab]crushing load,
[Db]Whose forms are [Bb7]bending [Eb/Bb]low,
[Ab]Who toil along [Db/Ab]the [Ab]climbing way
[Bbm]With painful [Eb7]steps and [Ab]slow;
[Ab]Look [Cm]now, for glad [Fm/Ab]and golden [Ab]hours
[Bbm]Come swiftly [Eb]on [Ab]the [Db/Ab]wing;
[Ab]Oh rest beside [Bbm]the weary [Eb7]road
[Ab]And hear the angels sing.
